atlas optimization-cascade

architecture optimization-cascade
  canonical_name OptimizationCascade
  owns CascadeStage
  owns OperatorSelection
  consumes SmallestSufficientState
  consumes CapabilityDemand
  consumes ResourceWeather
  publishes OperatorSelection
  publishes CascadePlan
  family optimization
  domain Optimization / Execution discipline
  layer execution
  semantic_question What is the cheapest operator that is still adequate for this decision, and has every cheaper stage already been tried?
  purpose Make cheapest-adequate-operator a planner discipline rather than a preference. An expensive stage is admissible only over the residue a cheaper stage could not resolve.
  maturity architectural
  node_types CascadeStage
  node_types OperatorClass
  node_types Residue
  edge_types narrows
  edge_types escalates_to
  edge_types precedes
  invariant never give a model the whole world when exact structure can first reduce it to the relevant few candidates
  invariant an expensive stage operates on the residue of a cheaper stage, never on the source set
  invariant stage order is measured per subject family, not fixed by doctrine; exact then latent then cheap-model and exact then cheap-model then latent are both admissible orders
  invariant a stage that cannot reduce the candidate set is skipped rather than run for completeness
  invariant elimination precedes every other stage; state that need not exist is not compressed, it is not created
  invariant deduplicate before compressing; content identity is cheaper than any encoder
  invariant a typed decision model is considered only when an exact bounded semantic residue remains and measured downstream work can be avoided
  forbidden_inference a stage existing in the cascade -> that stage running on every request
  forbidden_inference an expensive operator producing a correct answer -> that operator having been adequate to select
  forbidden_inference a cheap stage being wrong once -> that stage being inadmissible

stage s0-eliminate
  question Does this state need to exist at all?
  operator none
  note The only stage that can reduce cost to zero.

stage s1-identity
  question Has this exact content been seen before?
  operator BLAKE3 content addressing, interning, dedup
  precedes s9-compress
  invariant one physical body may carry many semantic references

stage s2-factor
  question What is shared basis and what is genuine exception?
  operator shared basis, typed binding, sparse exception, recursive structural factorization
  invariant an authority edge is never factored away
  invariant truth ownership is never factored away

stage s3-address
  question Can this be referenced instead of copied?
  operator handles, prefix dictionaries and tries, closure descriptors
  detail A deep hierarchical path is a projection. Hot execution carries an address handle, a subject handle, world bits and a closure mask. Stable content identity and small local handles coexist.
  invariant the pretty path is a rendering; it is never the stored form in a hot relation

stage s4-pack
  question Can this be represented densely?
  operator dictionary identifiers, enums, bitfields, bitsets, packed structs, columnar relations, adjacency arrays

stage s5-delta
  question Did anything actually change?
  operator Occurrence, FactDelta, incremental maintenance, temporal residuals
  invariant a small logical change produces a change representation of comparable size, not a new snapshot

stage s6-filter-exact
  question What is even lawful here?
  operator bitmap intersection, indexes, deterministic masks over authority, world, information policy and validity
  invariant this stage is exact and precedes every approximate stage
  invariant authority and world filtering never runs after a model has already seen the candidates

stage s7-cheap-cognition
  question Can a tiny classifier resolve this ambiguity?
  operator small local classifiers, sparse feature probes
  bounded_by cheap-cognition
  invariant runs inside an exact mask, never over an open world

stage s8-latent-reduction
  question Can similarity narrow this further?
  operator embedding neighborhoods, basis plus residual coordinates
  invariant narrows candidates; never decides authority

stage s8a-typed-decision
  question Does a state-bound set of atomic Choice, Score and Noul judgments avoid a more expensive operator on this exact residue?
  operator DecisionPlane over an exact shortlist, with a measured selective-value gate
  bounded_by decision-plane
  invariant the same state is assessed across independent questions; unrelated sources are not bundled merely to fill a question budget
  invariant unmeasured model confidence is not a correctness or savings certificate

stage s9-compress-physical
  question What is the right body for how this is accessed?
  operator Zstd with domain dictionaries, seekable frames, INT8, product quantization, polar residuals, FPQ families
  requires s1-identity
  invariant cold and hot tiers are chosen by access pattern, not applied uniformly

stage s10-borrow
  question Can this be read without copying it?
  operator Arrow C data and stream interfaces, mmap, borrowed views
  invariant a copy on the hot path is a defect until measured otherwise

stage s11-prepare
  question Has this cognition already been paid for?
  operator context cuts, exact source coordinates, prepared context and model state, reusable key-value cache
  invariant stable prefixes are prepared once and reused across tasks that share them

stage s12-reside-sparsely
  question Does all of this need to be resident?
  operator selective hydration, expert caching, residency policy under resource weather

stage s13-fuse
  question Are these separate physical stages for a reason?
  operator remove materialization boundaries, combine repeated operators, generated and native kernels

stage s14-prove
  question Is this still correct, and is it admissibly represented?
  operator semantic proof, authority proof, quality envelope, compression and copy receipts
  bounded_by optimization-proof

stage s15-lower
  question Has this compound become stable enough to become a path?
  operator recipe, capability graft, native shadow, native path
  invariant every lowering retains a lift or thaw path

metric copy_amplification
  formula bytes_copied divided by useful_bytes
metric hydration_amplification
  formula bytes_hydrated divided by useful_bytes
metric factorization_ratio
  formula explicit objects before factoring divided by bases plus bindings plus exceptions after
metric escalation_rate
  formula decisions escalated to an expensive operator divided by decisions entering the cheap stage

interaction cascade-reports-to-proof
  source optimization-cascade
  destination optimization-proof
  relation measurement_input
  preserves the stage at which each decision was resolved
  drops any claim that a correct result implies an adequate operator choice
  forbidden_inference a passing semantic proof -> an admissible materialization
